        "id": 121720,
        "name": "Medic-Tank",
        "username": "Medic-Tank",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/{size}/2107_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-06T01:22:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We could have a Promo Ranger where he reintegrated the timestream after the wonky place he got stuck in incap. Then we could have a promo power to do minute timejumps usable in combats where in effect it would allow a minor bufflike:</p><p>Timeslide: Another hero may play a card now</p><p>Mt bet timey-whimey things will get wonkier and a lot worse before they get better. Thus a not as anchored in reality Chrono-Ranger having more trouble maintaining time integrity could mark an evolution.</p><p>Cable is a superhero that comes to mind that uses time travel a lot but is far from static and I can't imagine Jim not learning from what he does.</p>",
        "post_number": 74,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:55:20.183Z",
